    public int findMostFrequentPixel(int[] pixels) {
        // Your implementation here
    }
}
```

For example, given the input array `pixels = {10, 20, 30, 10, 20, 10}`, the method should return `10` since the pixel value `10` appears most frequently (3 times) in the array.

```java
public class ImageProcessor {
    public int findMostFrequentPixel(int[] pixels) {
        int[] frequency = new int[256]; // Array to store the frequency of each pixel value

        // Calculate the frequency of each pixel value
        for (int pixel : pixels) {
            frequency[pixel]++;
        }

        int mostFrequentPixel = 0; // Initialize the most frequent pixel value
        int maxFrequency = 0; // Initialize the maximum frequency

        // Find the most frequent pixel value
        for (int i = 0; i < 256; i++) {
            if (frequency[i] > maxFrequency) {
                mostFrequentPixel = i;
                maxFrequency = frequency[i];
            }
        }

        return mostFrequentPixel;
    }
}
```

