import java.lang.reflect.*;

public class CustomURLLauncher extends URLLauncher {
    private static final String CLASS_FILEMANAGER = "YourFileManagerClass";

    @Override
    public boolean launchURL(URL url) {
        if (super.launchURL(url)) {
            return true;
        }

        // try first launch-method
        try {
            Class<?> fileManager = Class.forName(CLASS_FILEMANAGER);
            Method openURL = fileManager.getDeclaredMethod("openURL", String.class);
            openURL.invoke(null, url.toExternalForm());
            return true;
        } catch (ClassNotFoundException | NoSuchMethodException | IllegalAccessException | InvocationTargetException e) {
            e.printStackTrace(); // Handle the exception as per your application's requirements
        }
        return false;
    }
}
```

In the solution, the `launchURL` method first attempts to launch the URL using the `super.launchURL(url)` method. If successful, it returns `true`. If the `super.launchURL(url)` method fails, it then uses reflection to invoke the `openURL` method from the specified `CLASS_FILEMANAGER`. The method handles potential exceptions that may occur during the reflection-based invocation and returns `false` if both methods fail to launch the URL.

