public String smallestGoodBase(String n) {
    long num = Long.parseLong(n);
    for (int m = (int)(Math.log(num + 1) / Math.log(2)); m > 2; m--) {
        long l = 2, r = (long)Math.pow(num, 1.0 / (m - 1)) + 1;
        while (l < r) {
            long mid = l + (r - l) / 2, sum = 0;
            for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
                sum = sum * mid + 1;
            }
            if (sum == num) {
                return String.valueOf(mid);
            } else if (sum < num) {
                l = mid + 1;
            } else {
                r = mid;
            }
        }
    }
    return String.valueOf(num - 1);
}
```

This solution uses binary search to find the smallest good base for the given positive integer n. It iterates through possible base values and checks if the sum of 1s in that base equals the given number. If found, it returns the base as a string. If no good base is found, it returns n-1 as the smallest good base.

