protected void dump(Node node, JSONWriter w, int currentRecursionLevel, int maxRecursionLevels) throws RepositoryException, JSONException {
    if (currentRecursionLevel > maxRecursionLevels) {
        w.value("maxRecursionLevelReached");
        return;
    }

    w.object();
    PropertyIterator props = node.getProperties();

    // the node's actual properties
    while (props.hasNext()) {
        Property prop = props.nextProperty();
        String propName = prop.getName();
        if (prop.getDefinition().isMultiple()) {
            Value[] values = prop.getValues();
            if (values.length > 1) {
                w.array();
                for (Value value : values) {
                    writeValue(w, value);
                }
                w.endArray();
            } else {
                writeValue(w, values[0]);
            }
        } else {
            writeValue(w, prop.getValue());
        }
    }

    // Recursively dump child nodes
    NodeIterator nodes = node.getNodes();
    while (nodes.hasNext()) {
        Node childNode = nodes.nextNode();
        w.key(childNode.getName());
        dump(childNode, w, currentRecursionLevel + 1, maxRecursionLevels);
    }

    w.endObject();
}

private void writeValue(JSONWriter w, Value value) throws JSONException, RepositoryException {
    if (value.getType() == PropertyType.BINARY) {
        w.value("binaryValue");
    } else {
        w.value(value.getString());
    }
}
```

In the solution, the `dump` method is completed to handle the recursion into child nodes up to the specified maximum recursion level. It writes the properties of each node to the JSON object using the `JSONWriter` object. The `writeValue` method is used to write property values to the JSON object, handling the special case of binary values.

