```java
import java.util.List;

public class SystemDowntimeCalculator {
    public long calculateTotalDowntime(List<SystemEvent> events) {
        events.sort(Comparator.comparingLong(SystemEvent::getStartTime));

        long totalDowntime = 0;
        long lastEndTime = 0;

        for (SystemEvent event : events) {
            if (event.getStartTime() > lastEndTime) {
                totalDowntime += event.getStartTime() - lastEndTime;
            }
            lastEndTime = Math.max(lastEndTime, event.getEndTime());
        }

        return totalDowntime;
    }
}
```

The `calculateTotalDowntime` method first sorts the events based on their start times. It then iterates through the sorted events, calculating the downtime between consecutive events. The `lastEndTime` variable keeps track of the end time of the last processed event, and the downtime is accumulated based on the time gap between events. Finally, the total downtime duration is returned. This approach ensures an efficient calculation of the total downtime based on the provided list of events.

