private static int zzUnpackRowMap(final String packed, final int offset, final int[] result) {
    int i = offset; // index in packed string
    int j = 0; // index in result array

    while (i < packed.length()) {
        int value = 0;
        int shift = 0;
        int b;
        do {
            b = packed.charAt(i++);
            value |= (b & 0x7F) << shift;
            shift += 7;
        } while ((b & 0x80) != 0);
        result[j++] = (value & 1) != 0 ? -(value >> 1) : (value >> 1);
    }

    return j; // number of integers unpacked from the packed string
}
```

In the solution, we iterate through the packed string starting from the specified offset. We extract each integer from the packed string using variable-length byte sequences and store them in the `result` array. The method returns the number of integers unpacked from the packed string.

