public class UniqueCharactersChecker {

    /**
     * Checks if the input string has all unique characters.
     *
     * @param input string to check
     * @return true if the input has all unique characters, false otherwise
     */
    public static boolean isUniqueCharsOnly(String input) {
        // Assuming ASCII character set (0-127)
        if (input.length() > 128) {
            return false;
        }

        boolean[] charSet = new boolean[128];
        for (int i = 0; i < input.length(); i++) {
            int val = input.charAt(i);
            if (charSet[val]) {
                return false;
            }
            charSet[val] = true;
        }
        return true;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String test1 = "abcde";
        String test2 = "hello";
        System.out.println(isUniqueCharsOnly(test1)); // Output: true
        System.out.println(isUniqueCharsOnly(test2)); // Output: false
    }
}
```

The `isUniqueCharsOnly` method uses a boolean array `charSet` to keep track of the characters encountered in the input string. It assumes the input string is using the ASCII character set (0-127) and returns `false` if the length of the input string exceeds 128 characters. It then iterates through the input string, checking if the character has been encountered before. If a character is encountered more than once, the method returns `false`; otherwise, it marks the character as encountered and continues. If the method completes the iteration without finding any duplicate characters, it returns `true`.

