```java
public class IntersectingVolumeCalculator {
    public double calculateIntersectingVolume(List<AxisAlignedBB> boxes) {
        double totalVolume = 0.0;

        for (AxisAlignedBB box : boxes) {
            double intersectingVolume = calculateSingleBoxIntersectingVolume(boxes, box);
            totalVolume += intersectingVolume;
        }

        return totalVolume;
    }

    private double calculateSingleBoxIntersectingVolume(List<AxisAlignedBB> boxes, AxisAlignedBB targetBox) {
        double intersectingVolume = 0.0;

        for (AxisAlignedBB box : boxes) {
            if (box.intersects(targetBox)) {
                double xOverlap = Math.min(box.maxX, targetBox.maxX) - Math.max(box.minX, targetBox.minX);
                double yOverlap = Math.min(box.maxY, targetBox.maxY) - Math.max(box.minY, targetBox.minY);
                double zOverlap = Math.min(box.maxZ, targetBox.maxZ) - Math.max(box.minZ, targetBox.minZ);

                if (xOverlap > 0 && yOverlap > 0 && zOverlap > 0) {
                    intersectingVolume += xOverlap * yOverlap * zOverlap;
                }
            }
        }

        return intersectingVolume;
    }
}
```

In the solution, the `calculateIntersectingVolume` method iterates through each box in the input list and calculates the intersecting volume by calling the `calculateSingleBoxIntersectingVolume` method. The `calculateSingleBoxIntersectingVolume` method calculates the volume of intersection between the target box and each box in the list, adding it to the total intersecting volume. The final total volume of intersecting space is returned.

