You are tasked with implementing a dynamic proxy in Java to intercept method calls on a given interface. The dynamic proxy should log the method name before and after its invocation, and also verify the equality of the proxy object with the passed proxy object.

Your task is to complete the implementation of the `ProxyHandler` class, which extends `InvocationHandler`. The `ProxyHandler` class has a constructor that takes an instance of an interface `classAB` and an `Object` called `proxy`. The `invoke` method should be overridden to achieve the required functionality.

Your implementation should print the equality of `this.proxy` and `proxy`, the method name before invocation, then invoke the method on the `classAB` object, print the method name after invocation, and finally return the value returned by the method invocation.

```java
import java.lang.reflect.InvocationHandler;
import java.lang.reflect.Method;

public class ProxyHandler implements InvocationHandler {
    private Object classAB;
    private Object proxy;

    public ProxyHandler(Object classAB, Object proxy) {
        this.classAB = classAB;
        this.proxy = proxy;
    }

    @Override
    public Object invoke(Object proxy, Method method, Object[] args) throws Throwable {
        System.out.println("this.proxy == proxy : " + (this.proxy == proxy));
        String name = method.getName();
        System.out.println("before " + name);
        Object val = method.invoke(classAB, args);
        System.out.println("after " + name);
        return val;
    }
}
```

